Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:49:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 3224 imm32: user dictionary, conversion and candidates,
 WM_IME_CONTROL and hot keys of the built-in IME (CORE review)

The built-in IME answered most of its entry points with a FIXME and
ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED.  It now has what the documentation describes:

 - a user dictionary in HKCU\Software\Wine\IME\UserDictionary: ImeRegisterWord,
   ImeUnregisterWord, ImeEnumRegisterWord (NULL / 0 as wildcards, the last
   callback value is returned), ImeGetRegisterWordStyle (the EUDC style and
   one user style) and ImeConversionList (GCL_CONVERSION, GCL_REVERSECONVERSION,
   GCL_REVERSE_LENGTH); ImeConfigure shows a small dialog to register, list
   and remove words; ImeEscape answers IME_ESC_QUERY_SUPPORT, IME_ESC_IME_NAME
   and the EUDC dictionary path; ImeGetImeMenuItems reports no items.
 - the IME window answers the ten WM_IME_CONTROL commands (candidate,
   composition and status positions, composition font, open/close status
   window) through the input context.
 - ImeSetCompositionString takes the reading string and handles
   SCS_CHANGEATTR and SCS_CHANGECLAUSE; NotifyIME handles CPS_CONVERT
   (the dictionary converts the reading, an unknown reading converts to
   itself), CPS_REVERT and the candidate list actions (NI_OPENCANDIDATE,
   NI_CLOSECANDIDATE, NI_SELECTCANDIDATESTR, NI_CHANGECANDIDATELIST and the
   page actions) with the IMN_ notifications.
 - ImmSimulateHotKey performs the documented hot keys on the input context.

A layout that is not an IME layout has none of this, as on Windows: the
Imm calls for the dictionary, conversion lists, escapes and configuration
answer 0 and leave the last error alone for it (the todo_wine marks on that
in the conformance test are removed).

Also: ImmGetCandidateWindow read past the candidate forms for an index
over 3, and ImmUnlockIMCC answered TRUE for a destroyed IMCC since
GlobalUnlock changed (the conformance test imm32 passes on stock wine).

